## 🎨 Styling & Design Standards

### Tailwind CSS
- **Framework**: Tailwind CSS v4+ with dark mode
- **Color Scheme**:
  - Primary: `#4A90D9` (Blue)
  - Accent: `#F2901E` (Orange) - for dark mode
  - Dark: `dark:bg-gray-900`, `dark:text-gray-100`
  - Borders: `border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700`

### Component Styling Patterns

**Common Classes**:
```jsx
// Backgrounds
"bg-white/80 dark:bg-gray-800/90 backdrop-blur-xl"

// Cards
"border border-white/50 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-[16px] md:rounded-[20px] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md"

// Inputs & Textareas
"bg-transparent text-[13px] md:text-[14px] text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200 outline-none"

// Buttons
"px-4 py-2 text-[13px] font-bold rounded-xl transition-all"
"bg-[#4A90D9] hover:bg-blue-600 dark:from-orange-500 dark:to-orange-600"
```

### Typography
- **Sizes**: `text-[11px]`, `text-[12px]`, `text-[13px]`, `text-[14px]`, `text-[15px]`
- **Weights**: `font-normal`, `font-medium`, `font-semibold`, `font-bold`
- **Tracking**: `tracking-wider`, `tracking-widest` for labels

### Responsive Design
- **Mobile-first** approach
- **Breakpoints**: `sm:`, `md:` (768px), `lg:` (1024px)
- **Spacing**: Use `gap-`, `p-`, `m-` utilities with md variants

### Dark Mode
- All components should support dark mode
- Use `dark:` prefix for dark mode styles
- Test with `className="dark"`

